<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Yunus al-Harfush</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1625">1625</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Yunus al-Harfush was the most powerful emir of the Shia Harfush family, who held <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baalbek">Baalbek</a> and the Beqaa valley under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a>. He was at first an ally of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/druze">Druze</a> emir <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fakhr-al-din-ii">Fakhr al-Din II</a>, but the two later became rivals, and Fakhr al-Din's forces took Baalbek. He was executed by the Ottoman authorities in 1625.</p></div>
